{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "example", "parent_tag": "01RY", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Spec(\\mathbf{C}) \\to \\Spec(\\mathbf{R})$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Spec(\\mathbf{C} \\otimes_{\\mathbf{R}} \\mathbf{C}) \\to\n\\Spec(\\mathbf{C})$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathbf{C} \\otimes_{\\mathbf{R}} \\mathbf{C} \\cong \\mathbf{C} \\times \\mathbf{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\frac{1 \\otimes 1 + i \\otimes i}{2}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\Spec(\\mathbf{C} \\otimes_{\\mathbf{R}} \\mathbf{C})$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{example}\n\\label{example-injective-not-preserved-base-change}\n", "suffix": "\\end{example}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b022a88d6b861f78890b802dc02a18f334fad4527790a21ef2421c1e4df88a63", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d2895ec3f402ebf1b122e17e46cf1f0645cc1322cdf5c791c5aadb2424e7d672", "source_text": "Bijectivity is not stable under base change, and so neither is injectivity.\nFor example consider the bijection\n<MATH_0001>.\nThe base change\n<MATH_0002>\nis not injective, since there is an isomorphism\n<MATH_0003>\n(the decomposition comes from the idempotent\n<MATH_0004>) and hence\n<MATH_0005> has two points.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:631ace3a51b75c143391bcb026c24c2b363970f97eac06f1c7772fcaa88785bf", "unit_id": "tag:0496:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01RY", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nX \\ar[rr]_f \\ar[rd]_p & &\nY \\ar[dl]^q \\\\\n& Z\n}\n$$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$p$", "MATH_0004": "$q$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-surjection-from-quasi-compact}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:63a1348adfc8077abe0518be6e83503aee271f2ffd30248088d673d677877772", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:87614e8f01881b40a44b180bc8fd3f101407208932036c94213e1e593e2117a5", "source_text": "Let\n<MATH_0001>\nbe a commutative diagram of morphisms of schemes.\nIf <MATH_0002> is surjective and <MATH_0003> is quasi-compact, then <MATH_0004> is quasi-compact.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:435ef0eeefa6a732296652c1e175b6c746983fb2bb07042d97f127b4a00b77c3", "unit_id": "tag:04ZD:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01RY", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$W \\subset Z$", "MATH_0002": "$p^{-1}(W)$", "MATH_0003": "$q^{-1}(W) = f(p^{-1}(W))$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{topology-lemma-image-quasi-compact}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e3c5ca623ed83374ed48d01109e8c3dfc49f7d12e0b5955381a226e8e91a423e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9ce047a43d0213aeb6635a916feb420a06b9932e97032c41cbd7ce99c1aab9ad", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a quasi-compact open. By assumption <MATH_0002>\nis quasi-compact. Hence by\nTopology, Lemma <REF_0001>\nthe inverse image <MATH_0003> is quasi-compact too.\nThis proves the lemma.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2f9afb3b451c72e82be5677fde51df90dc393e9276ba396b1baa582ddde5aa24", "unit_id": "tag:04ZD:proof"}
